/* Reference values for `csa::modified_fm_rate`, at 60 digits.

   The range-Doppler-domain FM rate of Cumming & Wong, "Digital Processing of Synthetic Aperture
   Radar Data" (2005), Eq. 7.18 — the transmitted rate K_r corrected for the secondary range
   compression that the range-azimuth coupling introduces:

       1/K_m = 1/K_r - R_ref*lambda^3*f_eta^2 / (2*V^2*c^2*D^3)

   Bigfloats throughout so the reference is limited by the f64 the test compares against and not by
   this evaluation. The three cases are chosen so that no factor of the correction can be altered
   without moving a printed digit: D is away from 1 in A and B (D^3 is invisible at D=1), f_eta is
   negative in C (the square must survive it), and the correction is 0.67%, 2.3e-3% and 0.38% of
   1/K_r respectively — small enough that a focusing test does not see it, which is the reason this
   file exists. */

fpprec: 60$
c: 299792458$

/* The secondary-range-compression term on its own: the part K_r does not appear in. */
src(r, lam, f, v, d) := r*lam^3*f^2 / (2*v^2*c^2*d^3)$
km(r, lam, f, v, kr, d) := bfloat(1 / (1/kr - src(r, lam, f, v, d)))$

print("A  r=500e3 lam=0.30 f= 320 v=7500 Kr=2.5e13 d=0.80 -> K_m =",
      km(500000, 3/10, 320, 7500, 25*10^12, 8/10))$
print("B  r=800e3 lam=0.06 f=1000 v=7000 Kr=1.0e12 d=0.95 -> K_m =",
      km(800000, 3/50, 1000, 7000, 10^12, 95/100))$
print("C  r=250e3 lam=0.25 f=-450 v=7600 Kr=5.0e13 d=1.00 -> K_m =",
      km(250000, 1/4, -450, 7600, 5*10^13, 1))$

/* The five exponents, as ratios the test can assert without restating the formula. */
base : [500000, 3/10, 320, 7500, 8/10]$
ratio(a) := bfloat(apply(src, a) / apply(src, base))$
print("r doubled     ", ratio([10^6,   3/10, 320, 7500,  8/10]))$
print("lambda doubled", ratio([500000, 3/5,  320, 7500,  8/10]))$
print("f_eta doubled ", ratio([500000, 3/10, 640, 7500,  8/10]))$
print("v doubled     ", ratio([500000, 3/10, 320, 15000, 8/10]))$
print("D doubled     ", ratio([500000, 3/10, 320, 7500,  16/10]))$
